1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
Part 2

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,536
As chair of the town council subcommittee on park facilities, I'd like to bring

3
00:00:07,536 --> 00:00:11,345
you up to date on some of the changes that have been made recently

4
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:13,530
to the Croft Valley Park.

5
00:00:13,530 --> 00:00:17,847
So if you could just take a look at the map I handed out,

6
00:00:17,847 --> 00:00:21,000
let's begin with a general overview.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,206
So the basic arrangement of the park hasn't changed – it still has two gates, north

8
00:00:28,206 --> 00:00:29,250
and south,

9
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:32,000
and a lake in the middle.

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,575
The café continues to serve an assortment of drinks and snacks

11
00:00:36,575 --> 00:00:40,890
and is still in the same place, looking out over the lake

12
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:44,000
and next to the old museum.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,851
We're hoping to change the location of the toilets,

14
00:00:47,851 --> 00:00:52,284
and bring them nearer to the centre of the park as they're a bit

15
00:00:52,284 --> 00:00:56,797
out of the way at present, near the adventure playground, in the corner of

16
00:00:56,797 --> 00:00:58,000
your map.

17
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,267
The formal gardens have been replanted and should be at their best in a month

18
00:01:04,267 --> 00:01:05,010
or two.

19
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:08,408
They used to be behind the old museum,

20
00:01:08,408 --> 00:01:12,750
but we've now used the space near the south gate

21
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:17,556
– between the park boundary and the path that goes past the lake towards

22
00:01:17,556 --> 00:01:20,190
the old museum.

23
00:01:20,190 --> 00:01:25,274
We have a new outdoor gym for adults and children,

24
00:01:25,274 --> 00:01:28,810
which is already proving very popular.

25
00:01:28,810 --> 00:01:34,654
It's by the glass houses, just to the right of the path from the

26
00:01:34,654 --> 00:01:36,000
south gate.

27
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
You have to look for it as it's a bit hidden in the trees.

28
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:47,210
One very successful introduction has been our skateboard ramp.

29
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:52,200
It's in constant use during the evenings and holidays.

30
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:58,603
It's near the old museum, at the end of a little path that leads

31
00:01:58,603 --> 00:02:03,500
off from the main path between the lake and the museum.

32
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:11,800
We've also introduced a new area for wild flowers, to attract bees and butterflies.

33
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:17,023
It's on a bend in the path that goes round the east side of

34
00:02:17,023 --> 00:02:21,000
the lake, just south of the adventure playground.

35
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,886
Now let me tell you a bit more about some of the changes to

36
00:02:24,886 --> 00:02:27,000
Croft Valley Park.

37
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,750
One of our most exciting developments has been the adventure playground.

38
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:37,603
We were aware that we had nowhere for children to let off steam,

39
00:02:37,603 --> 00:02:44,480
and decided to use our available funds to set up a completely new facility

40
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:48,270
in a large space to the north of the park.

41
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:53,468
It's open year-round, though it closes early in the winter months,

42
00:02:53,468 --> 00:02:57,100
and entrance is completely free.

43
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:02,921
Children can choose whatever activities they want to do, irrespective of their age,

44
00:03:02,921 --> 00:03:08,240
but we do ask adults not to leave them on their own there.

45
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:13,127
There are plenty of seats where parents can relax and keep an eye on

46
00:03:13,127 --> 00:03:15,560
their children at the same time.

47
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:19,000
Lastly, the glass houses.

48
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,598
A huge amount of work has been done on them to repair the damage

49
00:03:23,598 --> 00:03:29,440
following the disastrous fire that recently destroyed their western side.

50
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:36,843
Over ￡80,000 was spent on replacing the glass walls and the metal supports, as

51
00:03:36,843 --> 00:03:39,250
well as the plants that had been destroyed,

52
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:47,004
although unfortunately the collection of tropical palm trees has proved too expensive to replace

53
00:03:47,004 --> 00:03:48,410
up to now.

54
00:03:48,410 --> 00:03:55,949
At present the glass houses are open from 10am to 3pm Mondays to Thursdays,

55
00:03:55,949 --> 00:04:00,320
and it's hoped to extend this to the weekend soon.

56
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:05,307
We're grateful to all those who helped us by contributing their time

57
00:04:05,307 --> 00:04:07,700
and money to this achievement.

58
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:09,000
The gardens have …
